Hey. I thought I told you not to call.

143
00:07:18,031 --> 00:07:20,325
[Doku-Gumi crew] <i>What,
did you forget about our agreement?</i>

144
00:07:20,409 --> 00:07:21,535
<i>Why is that damn horse</i>

145
00:07:21,618 --> 00:07:25,164
<i>still strutting around on the streets
at night like he owns the place?</i>

146
00:07:25,247 --> 00:07:26,165
<i>Well?</i>

147
00:07:26,248 --> 00:07:28,083
All right, take it easy.

148
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:31,920
Go sunbathing or whatever it is
you reptiles do to pass the time.

149
00:07:32,754 --> 00:07:34,256
It's all taken care of.

150
00:07:40,095 --> 00:07:42,014
[slurps, gulps]

151
00:07:42,556 --> 00:07:44,057
Mmm.

152
00:07:45,309 --> 00:07:47,227
[eagles groaning, panting]

153
00:07:48,687 --> 00:07:50,981
- [eagle 3] Are you okay, man?
- [eagle 1 grunts]

154
00:07:51,565 --> 00:07:53,734
What was with those guys?

155
00:07:53,817 --> 00:07:55,569
That shit was nuts.

156
00:07:55,652 --> 00:07:57,404
Hey, toss me one of those.

157
00:07:57,988 --> 00:07:58,822
[grunts]

158
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,074
[drink fizzes]

159
00:08:04,286 --> 00:08:06,079
Yo, give me some of that.

160
00:08:06,163 --> 00:08:08,582
You're the one who got us into this mess
in the first place!

161
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:10,542
Hey!

162
00:08:10,626 --> 00:08:11,919
- [grunts]
- [chokes]

163
00:08:12,002 --> 00:08:14,213
[high-pitched] I didn't mean anything
by it! Come on!

164
00:08:14,296 --> 00:08:16,673
- Hey, let's calm down.
- [both grunt, groan]

165
00:08:20,844 --> 00:08:22,804
- [burps softly, sighs]
- [can clanks]

166
00:08:24,515 --> 00:08:25,390
[gasps]

167
00:08:29,061 --> 00:08:31,522
[eagle 1 laughing maniacally]

168
00:08:31,605 --> 00:08:32,439
[yelps]

169
00:08:35,859 --> 00:08:36,693
Hmm.

170
00:08:37,611 --> 00:08:39,488
- Goddamn embarrassing.
- [both shudder]

171
00:08:39,571 --> 00:08:42,991
One can of Kines and that buddy of yours
kicked both your asses this bad?

172
00:08:43,075 --> 00:08:46,870
No, that's not it.
All this is from that old geezer.

173
00:08:46,954 --> 00:08:50,082
- Geezer?
- Yeah, some crazy old lizard guy.

174
00:08:50,165 --> 00:08:52,125
That freaky-ass, venomous old fart.

175
00:08:52,209 --> 00:08:53,252
[Yahya] <i>Venomous?</i>

176
00:08:54,545 --> 00:08:57,089
<i>It couldn't be. Is it really you?</i>

177
00:08:57,798 --> 00:09:01,426
<i>After all these years,
why would you show yourself now?</i>

178
00:09:02,177 --> 00:09:06,181
<i>You chose to betray me,
and you turned your back on the world.</i>

179
00:09:06,807 --> 00:09:10,143
{\an8}36 YEARS EARLIER

180
00:09:10,227 --> 00:09:12,479
{\an8}- [engines revving]
- [Yahya] Hey, wait up!

181
00:09:13,939 --> 00:09:15,649
Just take the damn thing, would you?

182
00:09:15,732 --> 00:09:17,943
[upbeat music playing]

183
00:09:18,026 --> 00:09:19,736
Don't just toss it around!

184
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,697
This is all so stupid.

185
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:23,699
Why was I the only one to get a medal?

186
00:09:24,241 --> 00:09:26,827
You were the one who noticed the fire
in the first place, right?

187
00:09:27,452 --> 00:09:30,497
If I were alone, there's no way
I ever could've saved that kid.

188
00:09:30,581 --> 00:09:32,165
How's that supposed to be fair?

189
00:09:32,249 --> 00:09:34,876
Don't get mad. That's just how it is.

190
00:09:35,752 --> 00:09:38,171
In that case, "how it is" can kiss my ass.

191
00:09:38,755 --> 00:09:39,673
[Gosha gasps]

192
00:09:40,257 --> 00:09:41,508
- [gasps]
- Ha!

193
00:09:41,592 --> 00:09:43,385
I should have done that
right from the start.

194
00:09:43,969 --> 00:09:47,681
Fancy medals like that,
they're not really our thing, pal.

195
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:52,603
[Yahya] <i>When I was young, I truly believed</i>

196
00:09:53,770 --> 00:09:56,565
<i>that I could move forward
without ever looking back</i>

197
00:09:56,648 --> 00:09:57,941
<i>because I had you,</i>

198
00:09:58,817 --> 00:10:03,071
<i>a partner who could make
my 350-degree vision a perfect circle.</i>

199
00:10:04,823 --> 00:10:08,535
Hey, Gosha! We're going to change
this screwed up world!

200
00:10:08,619 --> 00:10:10,203
You and me, together!

201
00:10:10,996 --> 00:10:13,165
<i>Together, there was nothing
we couldn't do.</i>

202
00:10:15,292 --> 00:10:19,546
<i>Back then, neither Gosha nor I
dreamt of becoming the Beastar.</i>

203
00:10:20,255 --> 00:10:23,550
<i>No, we wanted to be Beastars as a team.</i>

204
00:10:23,884 --> 00:10:24,885
[music ends]

205
00:10:24,968 --> 00:10:28,555
<i>But that night,
everything changed forever.</i>

206
00:10:33,226 --> 00:10:35,145
[jaguar chuckles]

207
00:10:35,228 --> 00:10:38,106
You've got great fur.
It's going to make me some money.

208
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:42,194
But, you know, I think I'll start
by removing your fangs.

209
00:10:42,277 --> 00:10:45,947
And don't you worry, darling,
you'll sleep through the whole thing.

210
00:10:47,783 --> 00:10:49,660
[gasps, grunts]

211
00:10:53,955 --> 00:10:55,874
[choking]

212
00:10:56,625 --> 00:10:57,459
[exhales]

213
00:10:58,043 --> 00:10:58,877
[thuds]

214
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,380
Looks like we made it just in time.

215
00:11:01,963 --> 00:11:03,674
[gasps]

216
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:07,260
- [chiming]
- [soft music playing]

217
00:11:07,344 --> 00:11:09,012
[Toki gasps softly]

218
00:11:09,763 --> 00:11:11,223
[Toki] Your scales...

219
00:11:11,306 --> 00:11:13,308
They're shiny like jewels.

220
00:11:13,392 --> 00:11:14,643
You're so pretty.

221
00:11:14,726 --> 00:11:15,602
Huh?

222
00:11:16,395 --> 00:11:18,230
Hmm. Huh?

223
00:11:20,774 --> 00:11:22,776
[soft music continues]

224
00:11:25,779 --> 00:11:26,780
[music ends]

225
00:11:28,115 --> 00:11:31,159
[Toki] Um, thank you for saving me.

226
00:11:32,619 --> 00:11:36,123
There's been a rash of these sorts
of incidents in recent days.

227
00:11:36,206 --> 00:11:39,418
Beasts are being drugged
with sleeping pills and skinned alive.

228
00:11:39,501 --> 00:11:41,128
You got to be careful out there.

229
00:11:41,837 --> 00:11:44,464
I see. So that's what this was.

230
00:11:45,006 --> 00:11:48,593
I suppose I was almost
turned into a fur coat, huh?

231
00:11:51,430 --> 00:11:54,850
[Yahya] <i>Within 24 hours,
she and Gosha were dating.</i>

232
00:11:56,601 --> 00:11:57,561
<i>And what's more...</i>

233
00:11:57,644 --> 00:11:58,478
SIX MONTHS LATER

234
00:11:58,562 --> 00:12:00,313
<i>...to my surprise, it lasted.</i>

235
00:12:01,106 --> 00:12:03,066
A lizard and a wolf, huh?

236
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:05,819
Man, talk about your unlikely
interspecies couples.

237
00:12:05,902 --> 00:12:07,279
[mysterious music playing]

238
00:12:07,362 --> 00:12:09,072
Do you even share the same values?

239
00:12:09,698 --> 00:12:13,368
If we didn't share those, we never
would've made it through six months.

240
00:12:13,452 --> 00:12:14,411
[Yahya sighs]

241
00:12:15,245 --> 00:12:16,997
So, you wanted to talk?

242
00:12:17,622 --> 00:12:19,040
Uh, I did, yeah.

243
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:22,210
I just found out that my girl's pregnant.

244
00:12:22,294 --> 00:12:23,253
What?

245
00:12:23,336 --> 00:12:24,421
The kid is mine.

246
00:12:24,504 --> 00:12:27,299
Huh? [splutters] Who's the father?

247
00:12:28,008 --> 00:12:30,260
I just told you. I'm the father.

248
00:12:30,343 --> 00:12:31,887
Yeah, yeah, but...

249
00:12:31,970 --> 00:12:34,055
You're oviparous, she's viviparous.

250
00:12:34,139 --> 00:12:36,266
You shouldn't be able to get her pregnant.

251
00:12:36,349 --> 00:12:38,602
The doctor said it was a miracle baby.

252
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:40,729
I have to support her.

253
00:12:41,271 --> 00:12:43,648
[splutters] You're joking, right?

254
00:12:44,232 --> 00:12:46,651
That delivery will be too risky,
and you know it.

255
00:12:47,569 --> 00:12:48,904
Hey. Listen.

256
00:12:49,446 --> 00:12:50,614
We were just getting started.

257
00:12:50,697 --> 00:12:52,699
This is no time
to run off and start a family.

258
00:12:53,366 --> 00:12:54,618
I mean, like...

259
00:12:54,701 --> 00:12:57,662
We still have to become Beastars together
and fix the world.

260
00:12:59,247 --> 00:13:00,207
[Gosha sighs]

261
00:13:01,124 --> 00:13:02,709
- Not me, I'm done.
- [gasps]

262
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:06,213
[Gosha grunts, groans]

263
00:13:08,673 --> 00:13:10,592
I thought that if we became Beastars,

264
00:13:10,675 --> 00:13:12,969
it would be a win
for peace and coexistence.

265
00:13:13,595 --> 00:13:19,392
But then, I found her, and I realized
she's the most important thing to me.

266
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:21,895
[sighs] So you're saying

267
00:13:22,771 --> 00:13:24,606
you're going to leave me on my own.

268
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,274
[Gosha sighs]

269
00:13:27,234 --> 00:13:28,318
[Yahya] <i>You traitor.</i>

270
00:13:28,401 --> 00:13:29,402
[music ends]

271
00:13:37,744 --> 00:13:39,329
- [device ringing]
- Huh.

272
00:13:40,163 --> 00:13:41,164
[mouse beeps]

273
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:44,960
<i>I've been looking into that wolf case,
and I got an update.</i>

274
00:13:45,043 --> 00:13:45,961
I'm listening.

275
00:13:46,711 --> 00:13:49,297
<i>It seems like
his parents are out of the picture,</i>

276
00:13:49,381 --> 00:13:52,759
<i>and his high school records
list his grandfather as his guardian.</i>

277
00:13:53,552 --> 00:13:55,470
<i>And wait till you get a load of this.</i>

278
00:13:55,554 --> 00:13:57,681
<i>That grandfather is a Komodo dragon.</i>

279
00:13:59,516 --> 00:14:01,685
[Yahya] <i>His eyes, those eyebrows...</i>

280
00:14:02,686 --> 00:14:05,564
<i>Huh. There really is a family resemblance.</i>

281
00:14:06,273 --> 00:14:09,150
Guess we need to dangle a carrot
and lure the kid in.

282
00:14:09,234 --> 00:14:10,360
[Corne] <i>Done and done.</i>

283
00:14:11,486 --> 00:14:14,739
UDON BEBEBE

284
00:14:14,823 --> 00:14:19,828
[Legoshi reading] <i>"I'm in trouble.
I need your advice. Bill."</i>

285
00:14:21,037 --> 00:14:23,665
- What could have happened?
- [Sunaga] Hey, Legoshi.

286
00:14:24,624 --> 00:14:27,085
- Uh, yes?
- I've been thinking.

287
00:14:27,168 --> 00:14:30,297
It's time for you to try making a delivery
to one of our aquatic customers.

288
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:32,507
Would you define "aquatic"?

289
00:14:32,591 --> 00:14:35,594
I want you to deliver an order
to a customer who is an ocean creature.

290
00:14:35,677 --> 00:14:38,054
Oh. Oh, yeah, one of them.

291
00:14:38,138 --> 00:14:40,223
Yeah, that makes sense. Uh, "deliver"?

292
00:14:40,307 --> 00:14:44,144
Our motto at this humble restaurant is,
"We serve all species."

293
00:14:44,227 --> 00:14:46,438
Just tell them you're from Udon Bebebe.
They'll get it.

294
00:14:46,521 --> 00:14:49,274
Uh, hold on,
they speak ocean language, right?

295
00:14:49,357 --> 00:14:51,276
[splutters] I'm not familiar with it,
so, uh...

296
00:14:51,359 --> 00:14:55,322
Oh, Legoshi, you're a Cherryton student.
It'll be no problem for you.

297
00:14:55,906 --> 00:15:01,536
<i>"Apupupoupi bebebe berobu ponporopoo."</i>
That's the only thing you have to say.

298
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:05,248
Huh? Okay, one more time.
Uh, <i>pep-pop, poo--</i>

299
00:15:05,999 --> 00:15:07,292
You sure I should go?

300
00:15:08,001 --> 00:15:12,964
MARINE ZONE THREE

301
00:15:17,302 --> 00:15:18,428
Hmm.

302
00:15:19,012 --> 00:15:21,139
Let's see here.

303
00:15:21,222 --> 00:15:22,933
Number four.

304
00:15:23,516 --> 00:15:25,226
Hmm, this should be it.

305
00:15:26,353 --> 00:15:27,896
[heavy clunking]

306
00:15:27,979 --> 00:15:31,775
- Then... I'm supposed to ring this?
- [dinging]

307
00:15:32,692 --> 00:15:34,694
[funky music playing]

308
00:15:36,196 --> 00:15:37,739
Okay.

309
00:15:39,824 --> 00:15:40,659
Hmm.

310
00:15:43,662 --> 00:15:47,874
<i>Okay, when we first make eye contact,
I say,</i> "Bogora bogora."

311
00:15:52,212 --> 00:15:53,046
[Legoshi gasps]

312
00:15:57,258 --> 00:15:59,594
[splutters nervously] <i>Bogora bogora.</i>

313
00:15:59,678 --> 00:16:03,848
[speaking ocean language]

314
00:16:03,932 --> 00:16:06,059
[sighs] Oh, man, what do I do? What do I--

315
00:16:06,142 --> 00:16:08,436
Uh, I brought you Bebebe udon.

316
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,896
You know, udon.

317
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,524
- Udon? Udon? I brought it for you?
- [fish speaks indistinctly]

318
00:16:12,607 --> 00:16:15,193
You placed an order with us,
dear customer.

319
00:16:15,276 --> 00:16:16,861
And I brought it-- Ow!

320
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:21,324
[gasps] Valued customer,
my finger is not a noodle. I--

321
00:16:21,408 --> 00:16:23,284
Please let go.
[splutters in ocean language]

322
00:16:23,368 --> 00:16:26,162
- [seal in English] Don't panic.
- [gasps] Huh?

323
00:16:26,246 --> 00:16:31,167
[seal] Ocean creatures,
they see movement, they try to eat.

324
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,211
It's normal.

325
00:16:33,294 --> 00:16:36,381
Just stay still and they'll let you go.

326
00:16:36,881 --> 00:16:39,009
Uh... I don't...

327
00:16:39,801 --> 00:16:43,888
Allow me to interpret for you.
It'll go a lot easier.

328
00:16:44,806 --> 00:16:50,353
[speaking in ocean language]

329
00:16:50,437 --> 00:16:54,441
[Legoshi] <i>That's right.
Seals are half land, half sea creatures.</i>

330
00:16:55,025 --> 00:16:55,984
- [chuckles]
- Hmm.

331
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:58,486
<i>This bilingual guy just saved my fur.</i>

332
00:16:59,029 --> 00:17:01,406
[speaking ocean language]

333
00:17:01,489 --> 00:17:03,783
[seal] He says, "I eat my udon."

334
00:17:04,492 --> 00:17:06,286
[Legoshi] Right. Here you are.

335
00:17:16,296 --> 00:17:17,756
[squeals, burps]

336
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,049
[Legoshi] Hmm?

337
00:17:19,132 --> 00:17:20,675
Wait, what about the bill?

338
00:17:24,262 --> 00:17:27,265
That bowlful of seashells becomes cash.

339
00:17:27,348 --> 00:17:29,642
- Take it to the exchange.
- The exchange?

340
00:17:29,726 --> 00:17:32,353
Seashells are the currency of the sea.

341
00:17:32,437 --> 00:17:34,230
They are valuable little things.

342
00:17:34,314 --> 00:17:36,524
Ah. I think I remember learning that.

343
00:17:36,608 --> 00:17:37,442
Uh...

344
00:17:38,193 --> 00:17:40,195
Seriously, thank you so much.

345
00:17:40,278 --> 00:17:42,906
You really, uh... You really helped me out.

346
00:17:42,989 --> 00:17:47,577
I am what you call a spotted seal.
My name is Sagwan.

347
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:50,872
You and I,
we live in the same apartment building,

348
00:17:50,955 --> 00:17:53,124
so we help each other out.

349
00:17:53,208 --> 00:17:55,502
Huh? You're in Beast Apartments?

350
00:17:58,546 --> 00:17:59,756
[Legoshi] That's incredible.

351
00:18:01,049 --> 00:18:04,636
Six months ago,
I was still living at home in the ocean.

352
00:18:04,719 --> 00:18:08,431
Now, I work, teaching the ocean language
at a big university,

353
00:18:08,515 --> 00:18:11,017
as I continue to study
the ways of the land.

354
00:18:11,101 --> 00:18:11,935
[Legoshi] Mmm.

355
00:18:12,727 --> 00:18:15,480
The land, I think it's a lovely place.

356
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:17,482
And I do quite like--

357
00:18:18,608 --> 00:18:19,984
- [groaning]
- Are you all right?

358
00:18:20,068 --> 00:18:23,029
You've got to keep an eye out
when you're wandering around like that.

359
00:18:23,113 --> 00:18:24,656
The land can be really dangerous.

360
00:18:24,739 --> 00:18:26,699
It's okay, I'm good.

361
00:18:26,783 --> 00:18:28,326
The ocean's no different.

362
00:18:28,409 --> 00:18:31,412
Uh, well, I guess
that's probably true, but...

363
00:18:31,496 --> 00:18:36,251
And besides, if I am to die, that's just
the way things are meant to go that day.

364
00:18:37,210 --> 00:18:38,378
- [grunts softly]
- What?

365
00:18:42,257 --> 00:18:46,427
[Sagwan] In the ocean,
a big fish will eat the smaller fish.

366
00:18:47,095 --> 00:18:51,224
And then, a bigger fish
will come and eat that big fish.

367
00:18:51,307 --> 00:18:54,102
Then, eventually,
that bigger fish will die.

368
00:18:54,185 --> 00:18:57,856
Then all the tiny fish and plankton
come to eat that.

369
00:19:00,233 --> 00:19:04,195
All the creatures of the sea,
we must eat and we must be eaten.

370
00:19:04,279 --> 00:19:08,491
We must eat and we must be eaten.
This is how we're all connected.

371
00:19:09,075 --> 00:19:12,162
Down there,
the word "devouring" does not exist.

372
00:19:12,245 --> 00:19:15,123
This is the harmony
that everybody lives within.

373
00:19:16,416 --> 00:19:18,418
"They must eat and they must be eaten."

374
00:19:19,169 --> 00:19:22,213
Yet you're telling me
they live in harmony?

375
00:19:23,047 --> 00:19:25,175
Whoa. [gasps]

376
00:19:25,258 --> 00:19:28,803
<i>I can't imagine that such a world exists.</i>

377
00:19:30,054 --> 00:19:34,809
<i>Here I am, tormented by my instincts,
trying to relate to herbivores,</i>

378
00:19:34,893 --> 00:19:36,311
<i>when right next to me,</i>

379
00:19:37,645 --> 00:19:39,022
<i>there's another world.</i>

380
00:19:42,775 --> 00:19:43,693
Hmm.

381
00:19:44,903 --> 00:19:47,989
[Sagwan] My apartment is number 501.

382
00:19:48,072 --> 00:19:49,741
Would you like to have some tea?

383
00:19:50,283 --> 00:19:52,994
I still want to hear your story too.

384
00:19:53,786 --> 00:19:56,206
Uh, yeah. Sure.

385
00:20:02,045 --> 00:20:03,129
Hmm.

386
00:20:07,634 --> 00:20:09,177
- [knocks]
- [Sagwan] Come in!

387
00:20:10,887 --> 00:20:12,347
Thank you for-- Whoa! No!

388
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:14,432
Legoshi, is everything all right?

389
00:20:14,515 --> 00:20:17,018
Uh, not exactly.
Uh, you... you got to put that away.

390
00:20:17,101 --> 00:20:19,229
[spluttering] I mean, please wear clothes.

391
00:20:19,312 --> 00:20:21,940
On land, you can't just be naked
around other people.

392
00:20:22,023 --> 00:20:23,733
Oh, good to know.

393
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:26,402
Well, I'll put clothes on.

394
00:20:26,486 --> 00:20:28,696
Please forgive me for any impoliteness.

395
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,573
Wait, hold on.

396
00:20:30,657 --> 00:20:31,991
Hmm?

397
00:20:32,075 --> 00:20:36,079
<i>I can't just impose my beliefs on him
in his own room, right?</i>

398
00:20:36,704 --> 00:20:39,707
You must find clothes uncomfortable,
Mr. Sagwan.

399
00:20:39,791 --> 00:20:41,709
You're welcome to stay as you are.

400
00:20:41,793 --> 00:20:43,211
[chiming lightly]

401
00:20:43,294 --> 00:20:44,963
[Legoshi] "Eat and be eaten,"

402
00:20:46,214 --> 00:20:48,341
but everyone still lives in harmony.

403
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:50,885
I just can't wrap my head around it.

404
00:20:51,803 --> 00:20:54,180
Here on land,
everyone's afraid of each other.

405
00:20:54,973 --> 00:20:57,976
Carnivores and herbivores
try so hard to keep their distance.

406
00:20:58,059 --> 00:20:58,977
[Sagwan] Legoshi.

407
00:21:00,270 --> 00:21:02,939
Did you experience
some kind of trouble, perhaps?

408
00:21:03,982 --> 00:21:04,857
There was a rumor

409
00:21:04,941 --> 00:21:08,403
that a wolf with a devouring record
moved into our building.

410
00:21:08,486 --> 00:21:10,571
Apartment gossip, I would say.

411
00:21:10,655 --> 00:21:12,115
But was that you?

412
00:21:12,198 --> 00:21:14,075
Hmm, so there were rumors, huh?

413
00:21:14,867 --> 00:21:19,289
Back in the ocean, I was a carnivore too,
just like you, Legoshi.

414
00:21:20,873 --> 00:21:24,335
In the ocean, everybody learns
how to live with their sins.

415
00:21:24,961 --> 00:21:27,755
Doesn't that weigh on you?

416
00:21:28,464 --> 00:21:29,799
It is not so heavy.

417
00:21:30,842 --> 00:21:34,637
When I look at this,
it feels like I'm floating in the sea.

418
00:21:34,721 --> 00:21:36,014
[chiming lightly]

419
00:21:36,097 --> 00:21:39,684
The balance is kept
because they are all connected.

420
00:21:41,394 --> 00:21:42,770
[Legoshi] Whoa.

421
00:21:43,604 --> 00:21:46,441
<i>When I'm with this person, it...</i>

422
00:21:46,524 --> 00:21:49,652
<i>it's like I'm conversing
with the ocean itself.</i>

423
00:21:51,321 --> 00:21:53,948
<i>It feels as if I'm floating, weightless.</i>

424
00:21:55,325 --> 00:21:58,703
<i>I think... I kind of like this guy.</i>

425
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

426
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

427
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,379
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

428
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,425
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

429
00:22:13,343 --> 00:22:15,887
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

430
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

431
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,561
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

432
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

433
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,611
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

434
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

435
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

436
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,791
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

437
00:22:44,874 --> 00:22:46,751
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

438
00:22:46,834 --> 00:22:48,002
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

439
00:22:48,086 --> 00:22:52,590
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

440
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

441
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,848
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

442
00:23:00,932 --> 00:23:02,809
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

443
00:23:02,892 --> 00:23:04,143
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

444
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:09,148
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

445
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

446
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,652
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

447
00:23:13,444 --> 00:23:16,364
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

448
00:23:17,365 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

449
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,372
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>
